From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] status/volume: the Sound page: outputs as chips, one row per playing app

Quick Options' sound sheet is the Sound page (lumaPresentation/soundPage.js):
the master volume as the main page's filled level, the outputs as a
two-column grid of chips (org.projectluma.AudioDevices1 version 3 labels and
kinds; more than four show the three used last and "More…"), and under
"Playing" one LumaUI media row per app with a stream
(lumaPresentation/mediaRow.js, drawn from the LumaMediaRow tokens): artwork
badged with the app, the player's title, where it plays or that it is
paused, its volume and a play key. A "Volume mixer" link opens Settings.
The device list of 0119 and the AirPlay picker stay as the page "More…"
opens, and as the whole sheet without the service or before version 3.

AppMixer gains playPause(), raise() (the Shell's own window for the app,
else the service) and setDefaultOutput(), and keeps the app's window title
for a player that names none. AppMixerRow and AppMixerSection go: no fader
strip per stream, no output key per row, no app without a stream.

quickSettings: a page may be plain (_lumaPlainPage: not a list in a well;
it may use the work area and fits its own list into it), may put a quiet
count at the header's end, and is asked before Back leaves it (_lumaBack).
popupMenu: the menu manager asks an open menu (handleEscape) before Esc
closes it, so Esc on the Sound page returns to the main page, and from
its full output list to the page.

AirPlay speakers found nearby are chips among the outputs (the picker's
receivers; choosing one connects it), looked for while the sheet is mapped.

The model is held only while the sheet is mapped; the page watches no
levels and runs no timers.

